<title>HUNGARY: Hungary revises March c/a surplus to $21 mln.</title>
<headline>Hungary revises March c/a surplus to $21 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary in March posted a current account surplus of $21 million and a trade surplus of $37 million according to revised figures pubished by the National Bank of Hungary on Tuesday.</p>
<p>HUNGARY CURRENT ACCOUNT (in million dollars)</p>
<p>			   Mar 97  Jan-Mar 97    Mar 96  Jan-Mar 96</p>
<p> Trade balance	     37	-402	   -180	-821</p>
<p>				(46)    (-393)</p>
<p>  - Exports	     1,682     4,489	  1,115     3,091</p>
<p>			   (1,773)   (4,580)</p>
<p>  - Imports	     1,645     4,891	  1,295     3,912</p>
<p>			   (1,726)   (4,972)</p>
<p> Services and income    -89	-174	   -129	-261</p>
<p>			    (-101)    (-186)</p>
<p>  - Tourism		  89	 159	     66	 118</p>
<p>				(86)     (155)</p>
<p>Capital investment</p>
<p>    income		 -171	-326	   -220	-445</p>
<p>			    (-170)    (-325)</p>
<p>Other current</p>
<p>    payments		 -7	  -7	     25	  66</p>
<p>			     (-17)     (-17)</p>
<p> Unrequited transfers    73	  99	     90	 256</p>
<p>				(74)     (100)</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Current account	   21	-477	   -219	-826</p>
<p>				(19)    (-478)</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Foreign direct</p>
<p>  capital investments   156	 371	    105	 451</p>
<p>			     (155)     (397)</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures in brackets were preliminary. Central bank trade figures are based on cash flow data, while Ministry of Industry, Trade and Tourism trade figures are based on customs statistics.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
